        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Vanderbilt University, Emory University, Methodist Episcopal Church\n- People: Cornelius Vanderbilt, John Emory\n- Places: Oxford, Georgia, metropolitan Atlanta, the South\n\nFacts:\n- Emory College was founded in 1836 in Oxford, Georgia by the Methodist Episcopal Church.\n- Emory College was named in honor of Methodist bishop John Emory.\n- Vanderbilt University was founded in 1873.\n- Vanderbilt University was named in honor of Cornelius Vanderbilt, a shipping and rail magnate who provided the school's initial $1 million endowment despite never having been to the South.\n- In 1915, Emory College relocated to metropolitan Atlanta and was rechartered as Emory University.",
